<title>USA: Ajinomoto pleads guilty in lysine case.</title>
<headline>Ajinomoto pleads guilty in lysine case.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ajinomoto Co pleaded guilty and agreed to pay a $10 million fine in a price-fixing case in the United States involving lysine, a feed additive, Randall Samborn, a spokesman for the U.S. Attorney in Chicago, said Thursday.</p>
<p>Ajinomoto was one of several companies accused of fixing the price of lysine, a supplement used in poultry and swine feed.</p>
<p>As part of its plea, Ajinomoto agreed to cooperate fully with the government's ongoing investigation.</p>
</text>
